http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/tabs-342.txt

All of the prizes so far have these properties (and possibly others): they
have immediate benefit, the benefit is permanent (or nearly so) and not
made obsolete by later guaranteed prizes, they are reasonably useful to
all classes that get them, etc.  So, I'm going to look at a few of the
other items that might make good prizes.

How about an amulet of ESP?  It has immediate benefit to everyone, and
remain beneficial long term.  But a number of classes get telepathy from
their quest artifacts (granted, a few get replacement luckstones -- but
not nearly as many.)  Close... but I'd be inclined to say no.

A +3ish hawaiian shirt or T-shirt might be a good prize.  That would have
immediate and long-term benefit to every class, and would not likely be
replaced later.  I have no reason (as of yet) to reject this.

Similarly, several scrolls of enchant armor would give immediate and
long-term benefit to many classes.  But, some classes have exactly zero
pieces of long-term armor by Sokoban, so this one is out.

A couple blessed potions of gain ability would also have immediate
benefit, and would be fairly useful to everyone.  But, I think this throws
off game balance quite a bit... it would suddenly make a lot more classes
able to cast spells.

A ring of slow digestion is overpowered -- it pretty much eliminates food
difficulties for the rest of the game.  The same goes for a ring of
teleport control -- if you get it, eat the next leprechaun, and all of a
sudden you've got insta-escape power.

An oilskin sack wouldn't really be immediately beneficial -- and certainly
not to the level a BoH is.  Underpowered.

A magic lamp would be way too powerful.  If there was another permanent
lightsource (other than sunsword) it might work, but as of yet there
isn't.

Those are the things that immediately came to mind reading the table.

