IN SUMMARY:
- the amulet of reflection does not seem to be an overpowered prize, so
there's no reason to specifically reduce its chances of appearing.  It is
useful, but not "too useful".
- it could make the game better to add more variety in the prizes, but
only if the prizes were very well balanced with the current ones.
- if another prize is added, it should have these properties: has
immediate benefit, has long-term benefit, won't be replaced by another
guaranteed item, is at least somewhat useful to all classes, and is
"balanced" right (ie, not too powerful or too pansy.)  Almost all of the
prizes so far (for any dungeon branch) have these properties, and the
exceptions (ie the Tsurugi) are already a source of much debate.
- looking through the full item table, the only item I can reasonably see
as a good Sokoban-level prize (with those properties) is a blessed +3ish
fooshirt.  There may be other appropriate items that I haven't spotted.



